The Atlas engine is fetched at build time from Atlas-Inf/atlas at the commit in
install/atlas-source.json (AGPL-3.0-only).

CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause) is fetched at build time. The image ships its notice
and the notices of the engine's Rust dependencies under /opt/atlas/notices/.

install/start-node.sh is adapted from SparkGLM's, whose container flags follow
LLooM's Atlas recipe (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 LLooM contributors,
LICENSES/MIT-LLooM.txt).

bench/sd_bench.mjs implements the decode-bench protocol of MiaAI-Lab's
sparkDash (MIT, https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash) and imports its
prompts from a local checkout at run time; no sparkDash code or text is
included in this repository.

Video decoding uses the FFmpeg command-line tools from Ubuntu's ffmpeg package
(https://ffmpeg.org). The qualified Ubuntu build reports GPL-2.0-or-later;
its package copyright and component notices remain at
/usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/copyright in the image.

The single-Spark Qwen3.8-27B variant (./start.sh --model 27b) downloads, at
install time, the Gated DeltaNet and attention projections (gdn.safetensors,
attn.safetensors) of TandemLLM's NVFP4 set for Qwen3.8-27B,
0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 at commit
ab09c92fa4a90d5cfd9d012fe92831c886efd9b2 (Copyright Khaled Bakeer; quantized
from Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B by the Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud). Those weights are
distributed by their author under the Apache License 2.0; their LICENSE and
README are kept next to the served overlay as TandemLLM-LICENSE and
TandemLLM-README.md. Only the weights are used, not TandemLLM's code (AGPL-3.0);
install/tandem_overlay.py, our own code, re-keys them to the checkpoint's tensor
names and re-expresses in_proj_z's block scales against in_proj_qkv's
weight_scale_2, the only change made to them.

With DRAFTER=dspine or DRAFTER=both, the same variant also downloads Tencent's
DSpine drafter for Qwen3.8-27B, tencent/Qwen3.8-27B-DSpine-b16 at commit
ea909c0f5fab8865f9e14600334f55f7ce47308f (Copyright (C) 2026 Tencent),
distributed under the Apache License 2.0 (its LICENSE is kept in the
downloaded directory; sha256 checked by install/check_files.py). The engine's
DSpine drafting kernels are written for Atlas from the DSpine method (Zhang et
al., "Draft in Parallel, Condition Through Depth: Adjacent Causal Injection for
Speculative Decoding", arXiv 2609.36173; reference code at
github.com/Tencent/DSpine, Apache-2.0); no DSpine code is included.

Model weights are not distributed in this repository. The checkpoints
nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local (the default) and
nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 remain under their publisher's licenses; see
docs/LICENSING.md.

The engine's NVFP4-CSF scale decoder and MXFP8 activation quantization follow
the formats published in vLLM (Apache-2.0), FlashInfer's b12x (Apache-2.0) and
NVIDIA Model Optimizer (Apache-2.0); see the engine's source for the
attributions.
